         "step": 1,
         "text": "For a curve described by the angle, \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{dy/d\\theta}{dx/d\\theta} \\), so \\( \\frac{dx}{d\\theta} = \\frac{dy/d\\theta}{dy/dx} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99049",
         "rule_named": "chain rule for polar slope"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substituting, \\( \\frac{dx}{d\\theta} = \\frac{1 - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2}}{-4 - \\frac{5 \\sqrt{3}}{3}} = - \\frac{3}{2} + \\sqrt{3} \\).",
